  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Perimeter Solutions has $343M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The company won 20 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $17.1M, and obligations are up 7.5% year over year. Obligations rose from $164M in FY21 to $343M in FY26, with intermediate totals of $106M in FY22, $89.9M in FY23, $248M in FY24, and $319M in FY25. The Department of Agriculture and the Department of the Interior are the top buying agencies in FY2026 to date, accounting for $227M and $116M in obligations respectively. Current-year totals are partial because the fiscal year is ongoing, and the figures above are contract obligations except where noted otherwise in award-value tables. This snapshot highlights where federal money is flowing to Perimeter Solutions and which agencies are the primary customers so far in the fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How have Perimeter Solutions obligations trended over recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "Perimeter Solutions obligations increased from $164M in FY21 to $343M in FY26. Perimeter Solutions obligations dipped to $106M in FY22 and $89.9M in FY23 before rising to $248M in FY24 and $319M in FY25. The FY2026 to date total is $343M, and obligations are up 7.5% year over year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which federal agencies buy the most from Perimeter Solutions?",
        "body": "The Department of Agriculture is the largest buyer, with $227M in obligations in FY2026 to date. The Department of the Interior follows with $116M in obligations in FY2026 to date. Those two agencies are the top buyers listed for the current fiscal year."
      }
